      {
        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "b54bc4cd-b1de-5ddb-9109-2d7baa68e9b3",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Films: Lt. Robin Crusoe, U.S.N.; The Apple Dumpling Gang; Truck Stop Women; Mackintosh and T.J.; Stay Hungry; King Kong; The Shadow of Chikara; Goin' South; The Wild Women of Chastity Gulch; Maverick; Bootleggers; Creature from Black Lake\n- People: Dick Van Dyke; Bill Bixby; Dennis Fimple; Russell Donovan\n- Companies: Walt Disney; Walt Disney Productions\n- Roles: U.S. Navy pilot; castaway; slick gambler; orphans\n- Topics: comedy films; comedy-western films; California Gold Rush\n\nFacts:\n- Walt Disney released and scripted the 1966 comedy film Lt. Robin Crusoe, U.S.N..\n- Dick Van Dyke starred in Lt. Robin Crusoe, U.S.N. as a U.S. Navy pilot who becomes a castaway on a tropical island.\n- Dennis Fimple shared the lead in the 1974 film Bootleggers.\n- Dennis Fimple had a role in the 1974 film Truck Stop Women.\n- The 1975 American comedy-western film The Apple Dumpling Gang was produced by Walt Disney Productions.\n- The Apple Dumpling Gang is about Russell Donovan, a slick gambler played by Bill Bixby, who is duped into caring for orphans who eventually strike gold during the California Gold Rush.\n- Dennis Fimple had roles in The Apple Dumpling Gang and Mackintosh and T.J. in 1975.\n- Dennis Fimple shared the lead in the 1976 film Creature from Black Lake.\n- Dennis Fimple had roles in Stay Hungry and King Kong in 1976.\n- Dennis Fimple had roles in The Shadow of Chikara in 1977, Goin' South in 1978, The Wild Women of Chastity Gulch in 1982, and Maverick in 1994.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
